{
  "_comment": [
    "FLUX 3 Image Klein (distilled) - IMAGE EDIT, 4 reference-image slots, 4 LoRA slots.",
    "2.502.0 (Tim: \"add flux 3 klein model\" + \"in edit image mode, show only models that can edit the images\").",
    "Built from the FLUX.2 Klein edit graph (Tim's upload of ComfyUI's template): each reference goes",
    "LoadImage -> ImageScaleToTotalPixels (1 MP, as FLUX 3's templates resize them) -> VAEEncode -> a PAIR of",
    "ReferenceLatent nodes (positive + negative chains); FLUX 3 reads the same reference latents ComfyUI's",
    "'Set Reference Multi Latent' appends. Picture 1 sets the output size (GetImageSize). In the prompt the",
    "pictures are <ref_image_0>, <ref_image_1>, ... in slot order (FLUX 3's own naming).",
    "Slots 81-84 and LoRAs 101-104 ship empty; bitGen Studio fills the ones it needs and removes the rest.",
    "AT LEAST ONE REFERENCE IMAGE IS REQUIRED. Distilled: cfg 1, 16 steps; for the BASE checkpoint set the",
    "style's Model to flux3-image-klein-base-int8-convrot.safetensors, cfg 3.5, ~50 steps.",
    "",
    "MODELS (ComfyUI's OWN folders; black-forest-labs/flux-3-image-klein-comfy on Hugging Face - gated, accept the",
    "FLUX Kommunity licence there first; free commercial use under USD 5M yearly revenue):",
    "  models/diffusion_models/flux3-image-klein-int8-convrot.safetensors   (distilled, 16 steps, cfg 1)",
    "  models/diffusion_models/flux3-image-klein-base-int8-convrot.safetensors (base, 50 steps, cfg 3.5)",
    "  models/text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_int8_convrot.safetensors   (CLIPLoader type flux3)",
    "  models/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors",
    "bf16 (11 GB) and nvfp4 (Blackwell only) builds sit beside the int8 ones - set the style's Model to use one.",
    "Needs ComfyUI 0.41.0 or later (FLUX 3 support). BFL advise a prompt upsampler: write a long, specific",
    "prompt (or let the app's LLM expand it) - short prompts under-perform.",
    "The scheduler is BasicScheduler 'simple' on the model's own sampling (model-agnostic core node); ComfyUI's",
    "own FLUX 3 templates are subgraphs - export one with Export (API) and use it as the workflow if it differs."
